<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Document</title>

    <link rel = "stylesheet" href="style.css">
    <script src="script.js" defer></script>

    <link rel="stylesheet"href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"/>

</head>

<%- include('partials/navbar') %>

<body>

    <div id = "home-gif-bg">

        <span class = "child-flex-2-center-close">
            <img class = "home-gif-img" src = "Photos/Astrorose%20Design%20Figma.png">
        </span>
        <div class = "child-flex-2-center-close">
            <p style = "margin-right: auto;" class = "home-gif-text">Save file editing,<br> <span style = "font-weight: bold;">made simple</span></p>
        </div>

    </div>

    <p id = "scroll-elm">Scroll to view more</p>

    <main id = "home-main">
        
        <div class = "flex-center main-problem-section">

            <span class = "child-flex-2-center-close">
                <img class = "main-problem-img" src = "Photos/Problem_section_photo.png">
            </span>
            <div class = "child-flex-2-center-close">
                <span class = "main-problem-container">
                    <h1>The Problem</h1>
                    <p>
                        
                        Editing game save files is often a tedius and manual process.
                        Players need to locate the save file, decode them using separate tools,
                        edit the raw data by hand, then re-encode everything correctly before
                        replacing the original save file. With such little margin of error,
                        one mistake could corrupt the save and break the game.

                        <br><br>

                        BackDoor simplifies this process by turning supported save files into 
                        editable fields, helping users make changes safely without needing to work 
                        directly with raw JSON or encoded data.
                    </p>
                </span>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class = "gif-section">
            <div class = "gif-section-container">
                
                <div class = "gif-section-container-inner">
                    <div class = "gif-section-block">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk icon-enlarge"></i>
                        <h3>Supported Uploads</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p>Import save files from supported games.</p>
                </div>

                <div class = "gif-section-container-inner">
                    <div class = "gif-section-block">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square icon-enlarge"></i>
                        <h3>Clean Editing</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p>Edit decoded values in a simple interface.</p>
                </div>

                <div class = "gif-section-container-inner">
                    <div class = "gif-section-block">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-file-export icon-enlarge"></i>
                        <h3>Export Safely</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p>Download a properly encoded save file.</p>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

    </main>

</body>

</html>